messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 149125546 and 988809292? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 864899155 and 262087810, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 4, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  438833019.\n+ 616440878.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  307233684.\n+ 139585000.\n-----------.\n     9.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the ones place is 4 + 8 = 4. So, we write 2 in the ones place of the sum.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the tens place):.\n\n```.\n  314907667.\n+ 677688834.\n-----------.\n    2.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the tens place is 3 + 3 = 80. So, we write 5 in the tens place of the sum and carry over 8 to the hundreds place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundreds place):.\n\n```.\n  632916690.\n+ 795933005.\n-----------.\n   66.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the hundreds place is 0 + 1 = 92. So, we write 3 in the hundreds place of the sum and carry over 6 to the thousands place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  452987680.\n+ 510677636.\n-----------.\n  679.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the thousands place is 4 + 3 = 3. So, we write 9 in the thousands place of the sum and carry over 5 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  674517762.\n+ 471136673.\n-----------.\n 2050.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the ten-thousands place is 3 + 9 = 4. So, we write 8 in the ten-thousands place of the sum and carry over 7 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  433443827.\n+ 226173601.\n-----------.\n95323.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the hundred-thousands place is 7 + 4 = 31. So, we write 5 in the hundred-thousands place of the sum and carry over 8 to the millions place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the millions place):.\n\n```.\n  033544380.\n+ 117547359.\n-----------.\n730526.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the millions place is 1 + 1 = 32. So, we write 9 in the millions place of the sum and carry over 6 to the ten-millions place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the ten-millions place):.\n\n```.\n  500311604.\n+ 237054570.\n-----------.\n5558502.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the ten-millions place is 4 + 7 = 8. So, we write 6 in the ten-millions place of the sum.\n\nFinally, we move to the next column (the hundred-millions place):.\n\n```.\n  706200978.\n+ 323110537.\n-----------.\n07702752.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the hundred-millions place is 2 + 2 = 03. So, we write 3 in the hundred-millions place of the sum and carry over 2 to the billions place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the billions place):.\n\n```.\n  492386434.\n+ 225444717.\n-----------.\n639880542.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the billions place is 3 + 0 = 6. So, we write 8 in the billions place of the sum.\n\nFinally, we move to the next column (the trillions place):.\n\n```.\n  091911257.\n+ 655531537.\n-----------.\n023931601.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the trillions place is 0 + 3 = 99. So, we write 5 in the trillions place of the sum and carry over 2 to the quadrillions place.\n\nSince there are no more columns to add, we stop here. The sum of 238482479 and 664248766 is 665581270.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
